      "key": "gg.hv.hc_ammo",
      "title": "High Caliber Rounds",
      "tier": "HV",
      "desc": "High caliber rounds are what the AS50 shoots: heavy brass-cased slugs that punch through armor. One of these rounds does more than a whole handful of rifle bullets.\n\nMake them in an HV Ammo Press from eight brass casings, sixteen stainless steel rounds and four gunpowder; a run gives you eight. NEI shows the recipe. Magazines are loaded with them in the same machine.\n\n[note]An AS50 magazine holds 10 rounds, filled from two high caliber rounds. A full stack goes a long way.[/note]",
